<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       Jawa_IonStun — the buildup-that-decays hediff that defines the weapon AND
       serves the capture pipeline.

       Behavior:
         * Each ion hit adds severity (via the projectile's HediffComp, see
           ThingDefs below). Severity DECAYS over time (SeverityPerDay negative),
           so isolated potshots fade — only focused / stacked fire pushes a
           target over the edge.
         * Low stages: minor consciousness drag (staggered, disoriented).
         * Top stage: Consciousness is forced very low -> the pawn COLLAPSES
           (downed) but is NOT killed (the ion damage itself is harmsHealth=false).
           A downed, uninjured pawn is exactly what CPERS: Arrest Here needs.
         * TIERING falls out naturally: mechanoids are separately hard-stunned by
           the EMP damage the instant they're hit; flesh pawns instead have to be
           worn down through these severity stages. Mechs drop fast, people slow.

       painFactor 0 and everything reversible => no permanent harm; the hediff
       simply disappears as severity decays back to 0.

       🔴 UPDATED, DROIDWORKS_ION_GUARD_1 (2026-08-30), design/Jawa/droid_ruling.md
       §5 Option A items 1-2 (items 3-4, EMP shield-break and body-size scaling,
       are deliberately NOT part of this change — separate items).

       Item 1 (let buildup apply to droids, not just flesh) was ALREADY DONE
       before this session started — DamageWorker_IonBuildup.cs's guard already
       reads `pawn.RaceProps.IsMechanoid`, not the doc's `!IsFlesh` (see that
       file's own history comment, dated 2026-08-12). droid_ruling.md §3/§5
       describe the guard's PRE-FIX state and are stale on this one point;
       corrected in place there rather than left to mislead the next reader.

       Item 2 (stay down longer) IS this change: `severityPerDay` slowed from
       -1.2 to -0.3 (the doc's own suggested number), AND a new "still
       overloaded" stage inserted at minSeverity 0.5 carrying the SAME
       Consciousness setMax 0.10 as the top "overloaded" stage at 0.9. Vanilla's
       HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay has no floor/notBelow field (checked
       against the live def dump - every vanilla user of that comp class exposes
       only severityPerDay/showDaysToRecover/showHoursToRecover/mechanitorFactor/
       reverseSeverityChangeChance/severityPerDayRange/minAge), so a genuine
       severity floor would need new C# - out of scope for a tuning-only item.
       This stage-based floor gets the same PLAYER-FACING result without touching
       code: once a target crosses 0.9 and decay starts pulling severity back
       down, it stays fully capped (not just "overloading") until severity falls
       below 0.5 - roughly triple the real time at -0.3/day vs the old top-stage
       band alone at -1.2/day. Judgment call, flagged for the owner: the doc only
       offered "slow decay" OR "floor stage" as alternatives; this does both,
       because both are pure XML/tuning and the combination is what actually
       reads as "stays down longer" rather than "collapses, wobbles, gets back up
       in under a minute."
  ======================================================================== -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>JawaIon_Stun</defName>
    <label>ion buildup</label>
    <description>An accumulating ionic charge disrupting the nervous system (or, in machines, the power bus). As it builds, coordination and awareness fail; enough of it drops the target where they stand. It bleeds off over time if the fire stops.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.55, 0.75, 1.0)</defaultLabelColor>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <isBad>true</isBad>
    <comps>
      <!-- Decay: severity falls ~0.3/day (~0.0125/hour) so a downed target
           stays down for hours rather than minutes. Was -1.2 (DROIDWORKS_ION_GUARD_1,
           2026-08-30, droid_ruling.md §5 Option A item 2). -->
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-0.3</severityPerDay>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>faint</label>
        <minSeverity>0</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.05</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>building</label>
        <minSeverity>0.35</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.20</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.20</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>overloading</label>
        <minSeverity>0.65</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.45</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <offset>-0.40</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.30</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <!-- FLOOR STAGE, DROIDWORKS_ION_GUARD_1 (2026-08-30). Same setMax as
             "overloaded" below, at a LOWER minSeverity, so decay from 0.9 does
             not relax the cap until severity has fallen most of the way back to
             0 - a downed target stays capacity-capped (still Downed), not just
             "wobbling back up", for the bulk of its recovery time. -->
        <label>overloaded</label>
        <minSeverity>0.5</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <setMax>0.10</setMax>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>overloaded</label>
        <minSeverity>0.9</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0</painFactor>
        <capMods>
          <!-- setMax pins Consciousness below the ~0.30 downed threshold:
               the pawn collapses, alive and unharmed, ready to be arrested. -->
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <setMax>0.10</setMax>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
